OL,3,AFamily of British explorer Sir Ranulph
OL,4,AFiennes say they don't know where he is
OL,5,
OL,6,FFamily and friends of renowned British
OL,7,Fexplorer Sir Ranulph Fiennes have said
OL,8,Fthey have not been able to visit or
OL,9,Fcontact him for months.
OL,11,FHis former sister-in-law told the BBC
OL,12,Fthat she did not know where he was, and
OL,13,Fnobody had been able to see him.
OL,15,FIt has been alleged that Sir Ranulph,
OL,16,F82, has been admitted to a number of
OL,17,Fcare homes under assumed names, after a
OL,18,Ffamily rift involving his second wife,
OL,19,FLouise Millington-Cotes.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/40
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
